"use strict";exports.id=1007,exports.ids=[1007],exports.modules={41007:(a,b,c)=>{c.r(b),c.d(b,{articleDetails:()=>d});let d={slug:"ideal-youtube-thumbnail-size",title:"What is the Ideal YouTube Thumbnail Size in 2025?",metaDesc:"YouTube thumbnail dimensions, file size limits, and aspect ratio requirements explained. Plus how to check your thumbnail meets all specs.",publishDate:"2025-06-23",category:"creator",categoryLabel:"Creator Tools",relatedToolSlugs:["thumbnail-size-checker","youtube-thumbnail-preview","image-compressor"],content:'\n<h2>Official YouTube Thumbnail Specifications</h2>\n<p>YouTube has strict requirements for thumbnail uploads. Violating these results in upload errors or automatic compression that degrades your image quality.</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Recommended resolution:</strong> 1280 \xd7 720 pixels</li>\n  <li><strong>Minimum width:</strong> 640 pixels</li>\n  <li><strong>Aspect ratio:</strong> 16:9 (widescreen)</li>\n  <li><strong>Maximum file size:</strong> 2 MB</li>\n  <li><strong>Accepted formats:</strong> JPG, GIF, PNG, WebP (as of 2024, YouTube officially accepts WebP)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Why 1280\xd7720 Is the Sweet Spot</h2>\n<p>YouTube displays thumbnails at multiple sizes across its interface:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Search results (desktop): ~246 \xd7 138 px</li>\n  <li>Home feed (desktop): ~360 \xd7 202 px</li>\n  <li>Mobile feed: ~168 \xd7 94 px</li>\n  <li>End screen: ~120 \xd7 68 px</li>\n  <li>Embedded player (max): 1280 \xd7 720 px</li>\n</ul>\n<p>At 1280 \xd7 720, you have enough pixels to display crisply at the largest size while maintaining reasonable file weight. Creating above 1920 \xd7 1080 wastes storage and file size without improving any visible size.</p>\n\n<h2>The 2 MB File Size Limit</h2>\n<p>This catches many creators off guard. A 1280 \xd7 720 PNG can easily be 3–5 MB. Before uploading, compress your thumbnail with our <a href="/tools/image/image-compressor">Image Compressor</a>. For JPG at 85% quality, a 1280\xd7720 image is typically 150–400 KB — well under the 2 MB limit while retaining sharp text and vibrant colors.</p>\n\n<h2>How to Check Your Thumbnail Specs</h2>\n<p>Use our <a href="/tools/creator/thumbnail-size-checker">Thumbnail Size Checker</a> to instantly validate:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Pixel dimensions (width \xd7 height)</li>\n  <li>Aspect ratio (is it exactly 16:9?)</li>\n  <li>File size (is it under 2 MB?)</li>\n  <li>File format (is it JPG, PNG, or WebP?)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The checker runs entirely in your browser — upload your thumbnail and get a pass/fail checklist in under 2 seconds.</p>\n\n<h2>Designing at the Right Canvas Size</h2>\n<p>Create your thumbnail in Canva, Photoshop, or Figma at exactly 1280 \xd7 720 px. This is the native YouTube thumbnail canvas. Export as JPG at 90% quality or WebP at 80% quality. Then verify with the Thumbnail Size Checker before uploading to YouTube Studio.</p>\n    '}}};